{"blocks":[["sops/","source-block-237","AWS/KMS - AWS Key Management Service",["sops","Key Features","Encryption Methods"]],["sops/","source-block-283","GCP KMS",["sops","Key Features","Encryption Methods"]],["sops/","source-block-296","Azure Key Vault",["sops","Key Features","Encryption Methods"]],["sops/","source-block-317","PGP",["sops","Key Features","Encryption Methods"]],["sops/","source-block-326","Age",["sops","Key Features","Encryption Methods"]],["sops/","source-block-335","File Format Support",["sops","Key Features"]],["sops/","source-block-363","yaml - YAML configuration files",["sops","Key Features","File Format Support"]],["sops/","source-block-404","json - JSON data files",["sops","Key Features","File Format Support"]],["sops/","source-block-436","EnvVar/.env - Environment variable files",["sops","Key Features","File Format Support"]],["sops/","source-block-486","INI",["sops","Key Features","File Format Support"]],["sops/","source-block-495","BINARY",["sops","Key Features","File Format Support"]],["sops/","source-block-507","Integration with mise",["sops"]],["sops/","source-block-539","mise/plugin/mise-sops plugin available",["sops","Integration with mise"]],["sops/","source-block-586","Can be used with direnv for environment variable management",["sops","Integration with mise"]],["sops/","source-block-654","Benefits:",["sops","Integration with mise"]],["sops/","source-block-668","Caching support for better performance",["sops","Integration with mise","Benefits:"]],["sops/","source-block-712","Flexible output formats",["sops","Integration with mise","Benefits:"]],["sops/","source-block-741","Works well with version control",["sops","Integration with mise","Benefits:"]],["sops/","source-block-778","Use Cases",["sops"]],["sops/","source-block-794","CICD pipeline secret management",["sops","Use Cases"]],["sops/","source-block-834","Infrastructure as Code configurations",["sops","Use Cases"]],["sops/","source-block-876","Team-based secret sharing",["sops","Use Cases"]],["sops/","source-block-906","Links",["sops"]],["sops/","source-block-918","GitHub Repository",["sops","Links"]],["sops/","source-block-975","Documentation",["sops","Links"]],["SOTA/","source-block-30","State of the Art (SOTA)",[]],["Sound/Diegetic/","source-block-17","Diegetic Sound or Music",[]],["Sound/Diegetic/","source-block-45","(of sound in a movie, television program, etc.) occurring within the context of the story and able to be heard by the characters.",["Diegetic Sound or Music"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/","source-block-39","Ambisonic Recordings",[]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/","source-block-64","Ambisonics is a full-sphere surround sound format that encodes audio in terms of soundfield directions rather than channels like stereo or 5.1 surround. It uses spherical harmonics to represent the soundfield in 3D space (horizontal and vertical directions).",["Ambisonic Recordings"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-0","5th Order Ambisonic Encoding",[]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-31","5th-order ambisonic encoding refers to a high-resolution spatial audio technique that captures or synthesizes 3D sound fields using spherical harmonics up to the 5th order.",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-211","🔊 What is Ambisonics?",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-247","Ambisonics is a full-sphere surround sound format that encodes audio in terms of soundfield directions rather than channels like stereo or 5.1 surround. It uses spherical harmonics to represent the soundfield in 3D space (horizontal and vertical directions).",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🔊 What is Ambisonics?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-518","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-569","The order of ambisonics determines how accurately the spatial characteristics of a soundfield can be captured or reconstructed:",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-705","Order 0: Omnidirectional (1 channel)",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-750","Order 1: Adds front-back, left-right, up-down (4 channels total)",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-823","Order 2: More precision (9 channels)",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-868","…",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-876","Order N: Uses (N+1)^2 channels",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-915","So for 5th-order:",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-941","Number of channels = (5 + 1)^2 = 36",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?","So for 5th-order:"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-982","This means 36 separate signals are used to encode directional sound detail.",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding","🎚️ What Does “5th-Order” Mean?"]],["Sound/Recording/Ambisonic/5th%20Order/","source-block-1062","🎧 Why Use 5th-Order?",["5th Order Ambisonic Encoding"]]],"format_version":5}